---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PrivacyBadge from '../../components/PrivacyBadge.astro';
import JsonLd from '../../components/JsonLd.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Merge PDF Files Locally — No Upload Processing | ZeroSend" description="Combine multiple PDF files directly in your browser. Reorder them and download one merged PDF without uploading source files for processing.">
  <JsonLd data={{ '@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebApplication', name:'ZeroSend Merge PDF', applicationCategory:'UtilitiesApplication', isAccessibleForFree:true }} />
  <section class="tool-page"><div class="container narrow-wide"><p class="eyebrow">PDF TOOL</p><h1>Merge PDF</h1><p class="lead">Combine PDFs in the order you choose. The source files are read locally by your browser.</p><PrivacyBadge />
    <div class="tool-shell" data-merge><label class="dropzone"><strong>Choose PDF files</strong><span>Select two or more files</span><input type="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" multiple /></label><div class="file-list" data-list></div><button class="button primary hidden" data-process type="button">Merge PDFs</button><p class="status" data-status id="tool-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p><div class="result hidden" data-result><div class="stats"><div><span>Files</span><strong data-count></strong></div><div><span>Total pages</span><strong data-pages></strong></div><div><span>Result size</span><strong data-size></strong></div></div><a class="button primary" data-download download="zerosend-merged.pdf">Download merged PDF</a></div></div>
    <article class="content-block"><h2>How to merge PDFs without an upload</h2><ol><li>Select two or more PDF files.</li><li>Use the arrow controls to set their order.</li><li>Choose Merge PDFs.</li><li>Download the combined document created in your browser.</li></ol><h2>Useful for sensitive documents</h2><p>Local processing can be helpful when you need to combine invoices, forms, reports, or other PDFs and would prefer not to send the source documents to a conversion server.</p><h2>Limitations</h2><p>Very large PDFs can exceed the memory available to a phone or browser tab. Password-protected, encrypted, damaged, or unusual PDFs may not load correctly.</p><h2>FAQ</h2><h3>Does merging change page order inside each PDF?</h3><p>No. Pages keep their internal order; you control which whole PDF comes first.</p><h3>Are bookmarks and interactive features guaranteed?</h3><p>No. This MVP focuses on combining pages. Files are limited to 50 MiB each, 100 MiB combined, and 2000 output pages. Complex PDF features may not be preserved exactly.</p><h2>Related tools</h2><p><a href="/tools/split-pdf">Extract pages with Split PDF</a></p></article>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  import { initMergeTool } from '../../scripts/pdf-tool';
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-merge]');
  if (root) initMergeTool(root);
</script>
